Subject: =?UTF-8?q?=F0=9F=92=AC=20Keep=20assistant=20replies=20visible=20w?=
 =?UTF-8?q?hen=20tool=20work=20folds?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Behaviours:
Exclude every assistant message from completed-turn folds, including replies
before tools and between tools in keyed and imported runless turns.

Keep each completed assistant reply from before a steer visible even when
later tools belong to the same superseded attempt. Preserve the whole-attempt
exemption when its last output is a reply completed before supersession,
including the deferred-work lastOrdinal guard. Fold tools only when that
whole-attempt exemption does not apply; retain interrupted-stream handling.

Integration details:
- The worked-for heading browser test keeps upstream's pointer-events wait and checks that Progress details stays visible.

Port to 965ddc1d6c:
- Upstream #28125 (Legend List 3.7.2) added the browser test that keeps following a streaming turn after its heading is expanded at the bottom. Its only folded content was an earlier assistant reply, which this commit keeps visible, so the turn had no Worked for heading and the test failed here while passing on 965ddc1d6c. The fixture now folds a completed reasoning entry and still checks that the list follows the stream after expanding. deriveTurnFolds did not change upstream.

Files:
apps/web:
- apps/web/src/components/chat/MessagesTimeline.browser.test.tsx
- apps/web/src/components/chat/MessagesTimeline.logic.test.ts
- apps/web/src/components/chat/MessagesTimeline.logic.ts

Tests:
- apps/web/src/components/chat/MessagesTimeline.logic.test.ts covers keyed/runless turns, completion, replay, expansion and collapse, deferred tails, pre-steer final replies during running and completed/expanded turns, and replies before and between tools followed by a replacement attempt.
- apps/web/src/components/chat/MessagesTimeline.browser.test.tsx covers visible assistant text across fold toggles and restores large-content scroll anchoring with reasoning rows and height/remaining-scroll thresholds above 500 pixels.
- Web focused suites: 138 passing (95 logic, 2 active tools, 41 Chromium).
- Restored pre-steer final-reply regressions fail before the fix (2 cases).
- Web typecheck, focused lint and format checks.
- Whole-stack focused validation on 965ddc1d6c: 1,321 passed and 2 baseline failures across 48 test files (every test file the stack touches plus CommandPalette.logic.test.ts and chatRouteCommands.browser.test.ts). Web: 679 / 32 files; desktop: 118 / 9; server: 432 passed and 2 baseline failures / 4; contracts: 36 / 1; scripts: 56 / 2.
- vp run typecheck passed in apps/web, apps/desktop, apps/server, packages/contracts and scripts; vp lint and vp fmt --check passed on the 119 changed files.
- Baseline: UsageService.test.ts on detached 965ddc1d6c fails the same 2 assertions (Pi /var versus /private/var path equality; Codex open-spy raw-path equality); no assertion was changed to hide them.

Scope: native mobile apps/mobile/src/lib/threadActivity.ts hiddenEntryIds is
unchanged because its separate React Native feed is outside this web/desktop
visibility change. iPhone/browser sessions served by Linux fork runtimes need
the next Linux runtime rebuild (r5), a separate follow-up.

Retire condition: when upstream merges an equivalent of 42b20aeff8
(origin/maria/fix-11353-assistant-text-visibility), keep only the
superseded-reply delta.

Model/harness: port to 965ddc1d6c: Claude Opus 5.5 / Claude Code.
